---
import ActionIcon from '../components/ActionIcon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookingCta from '../components/BookingCta.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Toronto Branding Agency for Product Brands | Ashbi Design"
  description="Work with a Toronto branding studio on your product launch or rebrand. See how Ashbi connects brand identity, retail packaging and ecommerce."
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="interior-hero container">
      <span class="eyebrow">TORONTO BRANDING STUDIO</span>
      <h1>Branding for product companies launching or growing in Toronto.</h1>
      <p>Ashbi Design is a Toronto studio led by Bianca and Cameron. We work with founders and marketing teams on the decisions that shape how a product looks on a shelf, in a retailer’s pitch deck and in an online shop.</p>
      <a class="button button-lime" href="/contact/?service=branding#project-brief">
        Tell us about your brand <ActionIcon name="forward" />
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="section container toronto-branding" aria-labelledby="toronto-branding-needs">
      <span class="eyebrow">WHEN TO BRING US IN</span>
      <h2 id="toronto-branding-needs">What are you getting ready for?</h2>
      <div class="toronto-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Pitching a retailer</h3>
          <p>Bring the pack format, planned flavours or variants, and any buyer requirements you already have. We can align the identity, packaging and sell sheet so a buyer can see what the product is and how the range fits together.</p>
          <a href="/services/packaging-design-services/">Explore packaging design</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Launching online</h3>
          <p>Give customers a clear reason to buy from a small product photo. We design the brand and its online applications together, from product imagery to the way you explain the differences between variants.</p>
          <a href="/services/web-design/">Explore web design</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Refreshing an existing brand</h3>
          <p>Show us the labels, assets and channels your customers already recognise. We can identify what to keep, what has stopped working and which materials need to change first.</p>
          <a href="/services/branding/">Explore brand strategy and identity</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section container toronto-branding" aria-labelledby="toronto-branding-work">
      <span class="eyebrow">SELECTED PRODUCT WORK</span>
      <h2 id="toronto-branding-work">See how the identity carries across formats.</h2>
      <div class="toronto-grid toronto-work">
        <article>
          <h3>CocoFro</h3>
          <p>Brand identity, packaging artwork and product renders for a freeze-dried dessert range. Distinct colours help set the flavours apart while the packs still read as one range.</p>
          <a href="/branding-projects/cocofro/">View the CocoFro case study</a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Marin Food</h3>
          <p>Brand identity and packaging for a gourmet butter range, carried into its website, sell sheets and brand deck.</p>
          <a href="/branding-projects/marin-food/">View the Marin Food case study</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <BookingCta service="branding" />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .toronto-branding h2 {
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .toronto-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .toronto-work {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .toronto-grid article {
    border-top: 1px solid currentColor;
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .toronto-grid a {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 8px;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 740px) {
    .toronto-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
